            <ArticleTitle>Medication safety in rehabilitation medicine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>271-303</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pmr.2012.02.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rehabilitation medicine is practiced in a variety of settings. Physiatrists are an integral part of the care provided in many of these settings and are often consulted to provide diagnostic and therapeutic services and expertise to individuals with a variety of diagnoses. In this role, it is imperative that physiatrists have a working knowledge of various medications as well as the principles of medication safety. This article provides a foundation in the general and specific aspects of medication safety as they apply to the practice of rehabilitation medicine.</AbstractText>
